licence; there is no copyleft (no GPL, LGPL, AGPL, MPL, or SSPL) anywhere in the
dependency tree. Audited 2026-08-09 with `cargo-license` over the non-dev,
non-build dependency graph:

    156  Apache-2.0 OR MIT
     48  MIT
     19  Apache-2.0
     19  other permissive (ISC, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, Unlicense, Zlib,
         BSL-1.0, 0BSD, Unicode-3.0, Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception)

Most of those are dual-licensed `Apache-2.0 OR MIT`, which llm-proxy takes under
Apache-2.0. The crates below are different: their licences apply conjunctively
(`AND`) or are ISC/BSD, all of which require the copyright notice and disclaimer
to be reproduced in redistributions, including binary ones. Their notices are
therefore reproduced in full here.

    matchit          0.7.3     BSD-3-Clause AND MIT
    ring             0.17.14   Apache-2.0 AND ISC
    rustls-webpki    0.103.13  ISC
    subtle           2.6.1     BSD-3-Clause
    unicode-ident    1.0.24    (Apache-2.0 OR MIT) AND Unicode-3.0
    untrusted        0.9.0     ISC

The full licence text for each is in that crate's source distribution, under
`~/.cargo/registry/src/*/<crate>-<version>/`. **Before publishing a binary
release, those texts must be copied into this file or into an accompanying
THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES file** — a list of crate names is not sufficient to satisfy
a BSD or ISC notice requirement. This file records the audit and the obligation;
it does not yet discharge it, and saying so is the point.

